  "slug": "association-adjusting-2e22",
  "summary": "New resources extend GWAS locus resolution to RNA features, single-cell chromatin, and a 657-dataset IGVF knowledge graph, alongside LD references for admixed cohorts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is assigning GWAS loci to effector genes and the cellular contexts in which they act. A multi-layer colocalization of 338 T2D fine-mapped signals with GTEx adipose data goes beyond expression to exon, transcript and splice-junction usage. CellColocDB offers coloc.abf colocalization across bulk, sorted-cell and single-cell data, while EPIC2 links GWAS summary statistics to single-cell chromatin accessibility, accounting for LD, to rank trait-relevant cell types. The IGVF Catalog integrates 657 variant-function datasets into a knowledge graph with APIs and an LLM interface. PRS-LDmix (ancestry-mixed LD panels for PRS-CS), a mouse pangenome graph reference, and Pooch for parent-of-origin classification address adjacent genomic infrastructure rather than effector-gene assignment directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
